1	// IcountTrigger is the F6 sibling of CsrTrigger: instead of pattern-matching
2	// a magic csrw, it counts committed insns and fires HYBRID_HANDOFF_EXIT once
3	// the per-hart counter reaches the configured target. Lets vsim drain at an
4	// arbitrary dynamic-insn position - the foundation for SimPoint slice-consume
5	// (F11) and orchestrator-driven icount switching.
6	//
7	// Duck-typed interface contract (matches CsrTrigger so HandoffController's
8	// template instantiation works for both):
9	//   - lookup(pc) -> std::optional<CsrTriggerHit>
10	//   - empty()    -> bool
11	//   - observe_commit() -> void   (icount-specific; HandoffController calls
12	//                                 via if-constexpr requires-clause)
