282	  // icount-trigger variant: drain after `target` committed insns retire,
283	  // regardless of PC. Sibling to enable_hybrid_handoff (which is CSR/PC). The
284	  // two modes are mutually exclusive on a single run -- callers pass at most
285	  // one. Multi-hart out of scope per F6: the trigger counts hart-0 retires.
286	  void enable_hybrid_icount_handoff(const std::string& state_out_path,
